      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redwood%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early pioneers settled Redwood during the mid-nineteenth century, drawn by gold discoveries and the fertile Rogue River Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/redwood_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gold found along Josephine Creek in May 1851 brought hundreds of miners and settlers to the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/redwood_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early farms in Redwood focused on irrigation ditches and the production of wheat, fruits, and vegetables.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/redwood_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community of Redwood sits at an elevation of 935 feet above sea level.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redwood%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Redwood experienced significant territorial changes in the early 2000s due to annexation by the neighboring city of Grants Pass.",
